WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.161 --> 00:00:15.084
Two weeks had passed since Anne arrived at Green Gables.

2
00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:20.248
She had been very busy, acquainting herself with every tree, shrub, and plant.

3
00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:24.592
After her discoveries Anne would run home and tell Matthew and Marilla.

4
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:28.776
Matthew listened to it all with a smile of enjoyment on his face.

5
00:00:29.436 --> 00:00:35.739
Marilla listened until she found herself becoming too interested in Anne's adventures, and then she told Anne to

6
00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:36.399
be quiet.

7
00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:40.501
Anne was in the orchard one day when the busybody Mrs.

8
00:00:40.581 --> 00:00:42.241
Lynde arrived to inspect her.

9
00:00:42.802 --> 00:00:47.384
Mrs. Lynde said to Marilla, "I've heard all about your orphan.

10
00:00:48.004 --> 00:00:49.685
It's too bad there was a mistake.

11
00:00:50.305 --> 00:00:51.505
Can't you send her back?"

12
00:00:52.126 --> 00:00:54.407
"We could, but we decided not to.

13
00:00:55.047 --> 00:01:00.342
Matthew liked her, and I must say, I like her too, though she's not perfect.

14
00:01:00.943 --> 00:01:03.104
The house is a different place already.

15
00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:04.846
She's a bright little thing."

16
00:01:06.127 --> 00:01:09.509
"You have no experience with children, Marilla," Mrs.

17
00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.991
Lynde said, "and you can't guess how she'll be.

18
00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.054
I just hope the situation will be all right."

19
00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:19.097
"I'm not discouraged," was Marilla's dry response.

20
00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:22.219
"I suppose you'd like to see Anne.

21
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.460
I'll call her."

22
00:01:24.201 --> 00:01:27.564
Anne ran in with her face flushed from her adventures in the orchard.

23
00:01:28.064 --> 00:01:32.586
But the presence of a stranger was unexpected, and Anne was suddenly shy.

24
00:01:33.246 --> 00:01:34.347
She stood near the door.

25
00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.728
Anne certainly was an odd-looking girl.

26
00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:43.831
She wore the old, ill-fitting dress from the orphanage, and her hair was messy from running around.

27
00:01:43.851 --> 00:01:47.372
"They didn't choose you for your looks, that's for sure!"

28
00:01:47.772 --> 00:01:48.472
began Mrs.

29
00:01:48.532 --> 00:01:51.634
Lynde. "She's very skinny and plain, Marilla.

30
00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:54.095
Come here, child, and let me look at you.

31
00:01:54.775 --> 00:01:56.736
How many freckles does she have?

32
00:01:57.448 --> 00:01:59.149
And hair as red as carrots!

33
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.951
Come closer, child."

34
00:02:02.231 --> 00:02:05.854
Anne came closer but not exactly in the manner that Mrs.

35
00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:06.895
Lynde expected.

36
00:02:07.515 --> 00:02:10.397
With one jump Anne stood in front of Mrs.

37
00:02:10.477 --> 00:02:15.580
Lynde. Anne's face was red with anger, and she trembled from head to toe.

38
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.364
"I hate you," she said angrily, stamping her foot on the floor.

39
00:02:20.384 --> 00:02:23.666
"I hate you, I hate you, I hate you!"

40
00:02:24.306 --> 00:02:26.548
She stamped louder each time she spoke.

41
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.421
"How dare you call me ugly and skinny?

42
00:02:30.961 --> 00:02:33.502
How dare you say I have freckles and red hair?

43
00:02:34.082 --> 00:02:36.443
You are a rude, unfeeling woman!"

44
00:02:36.463 --> 00:02:40.024
"Anne!" Marilla gasped.

45
00:02:40.584 --> 00:02:43.845
But Anne was not daunted and continued to face Mrs.

46
00:02:43.925 --> 00:02:46.426
Lynde with her head up and her eyes furious.

47
00:02:46.446 --> 00:02:49.787
"How dare you say such things about me?"

48
00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.748
she cried in a choked voice.

49
00:02:52.788 --> 00:02:58.332
"How would you like to be told you are fat and clumsy and probably don't have any imagination?

50
00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.433
I hope I hurt your feelings.

51
00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.156
I will never forgive you, never, never!"

52
00:03:04.876 --> 00:03:06.097
Stamp, stamp!

53
00:03:06.798 --> 00:03:09.459
"Did you ever see such a terrible temper!"

54
00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.561
exclaimed the horrified Mrs.

55
00:03:11.641 --> 00:03:17.265
Lynde. "Anne, go to your room and stay there until I come up!"

56
00:03:17.685 --> 00:03:21.608
Marilla said, recovering her powers of speech with some difficulty.

57
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:28.843
Anne burst into tears, ran through the hall, up the stairs, and slammed the bedroom door.

58
00:03:28.863 --> 00:03:32.245
"Well, good luck with her," said Mrs.

59
00:03:32.325 --> 00:03:37.128
Lynde. "You shouldn't have said those things about her, Rachel," Marilla said.

60
00:03:37.148 --> 00:03:39.209
"What?" said Mrs.

61
00:03:39.269 --> 00:03:42.190
Lynde. "Whose side are you on, Marilla?"

62
00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:46.433
"I'm not trying to excuse her," said Marilla slowly.

63
00:03:46.453 --> 00:03:48.734
"She was very naughty.

64
00:03:49.254 --> 00:03:52.576
But nobody has taught Anne what is right.

65
00:03:53.404 --> 00:03:55.786
And you did say too much, Rachel."

66
00:03:55.806 --> 00:03:59.928
"I will be very careful when I visit again, Marilla.

67
00:04:00.468 --> 00:04:03.550
An orphan is more important than I am, that's clear!"

68
00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:04.530
said Mrs.

69
00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.952
Lynde and walked out the door in a huff.

70
00:04:08.473 --> 00:04:12.635
Marilla went upstairs, where she found Anne face-down on the bed, crying.

71
00:04:13.555 --> 00:04:15.056
"Anne," said Marilla.

72
00:04:15.817 --> 00:04:16.717
There was no answer.

73
00:04:16.737 --> 00:04:19.339
"Anne," Marilla said louder.

74
00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.500
"Get off the bed and listen now!"

75
00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.841
Anne sat up and looked at the floor.

76
00:04:23.861 --> 00:04:29.742
"Mrs. Lynde will certainly have a nice story about you to tell everyone," Marilla went on.

77
00:04:29.762 --> 00:04:32.803
"You must go and say sorry to Mrs.

78
00:04:32.863 --> 00:04:35.764
Lynde. You must ask her to forgive you."

79
00:04:35.784 --> 00:04:39.145
"I can never say sorry," said Anne.

80
00:04:39.165 --> 00:04:41.346
"You can punish me, Marilla.

81
00:04:41.906 --> 00:04:46.947
You can put me in a deep, dark dungeon with snakes and feed me bread and water.

82
00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.228
I will not say sorry."

83
00:04:50.264 --> 00:04:52.905
"There aren't any dungeons in Avonlea.

84
00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:57.207
But you will stay in your room until you say sorry to Mrs.

85
00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:01.309
Lynde." "Then I will stay here forever," Anne replied.

86
00:05:01.329 --> 00:05:03.189
"I am not sorry.

87
00:05:03.209 --> 00:05:05.630
I am happy I said those things!"

88
00:05:06.471 --> 00:05:08.231
At that, Marilla left the room.

89
00:05:10.112 --> 00:05:16.635
Downstairs, Marilla told Matthew the story, impressing upon him the seriousness of Anne's misbehavior.

90
00:05:16.655 --> 00:05:19.236
"Mrs. Lynde is an old gossip!"

91
00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.660
Matthew retorted.

92
00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.521
"Matthew! I'm astonished!

93
00:05:24.221 --> 00:05:26.102
Don't you think Anne should be punished?"

94
00:05:26.542 --> 00:05:27.362
Marilla asked.

95
00:05:28.843 --> 00:05:31.043
"Yes, of course," Matthew answered.

96
00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:32.524
"But not too much.

97
00:05:33.264 --> 00:05:35.785
You will give her something to eat while she stays in her room?"

98
00:05:35.805 --> 00:05:38.905
"When do I starve people, Matthew?"

99
00:05:39.406 --> 00:05:40.606
said Marilla angrily.

100
00:05:40.626 --> 00:05:43.627
"Matthew was no help," she thought.

101
00:05:44.387 --> 00:05:47.668
Marilla brought breakfast, lunch, and dinner to Anne's bedroom.

102
00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.841
Anne still did not want to say sorry.

103
00:05:51.921 --> 00:05:54.282
Matthew crept upstairs and went to her room.

104
00:05:54.302 --> 00:05:57.363
"Anne," he whispered, "how are you?"

105
00:05:58.063 --> 00:05:58.743
"I'm all right.

106
00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:00.483
It is lonely, though."

107
00:06:01.164 --> 00:06:05.765
Anne smiled sadly, thinking of the many years she would stay in the room.

108
00:06:05.785 --> 00:06:08.606
"Anne, how about you say sorry soon?"

109
00:06:09.086 --> 00:06:10.186
Matthew whispered again.

110
00:06:10.206 --> 00:06:14.127
"Well, I am sorry now," Anne admitted.

111
00:06:14.147 --> 00:06:15.808
"But I can't tell Mrs.

112
00:06:16.812 --> 00:06:18.973
Lynde. It would be so humiliating.

113
00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:23.136
But I will do anything for you, if you really want me to."

114
00:06:23.156 --> 00:06:25.597
"Of course I want you to say sorry.

115
00:06:26.237 --> 00:06:27.838
It's too quiet without you, Anne.

116
00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:31.040
Just go and say sorry, there's a good girl."

117
00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:33.261
"Very well," said Anne.

118
00:06:33.281 --> 00:06:35.503
"But don't tell Marilla I asked you."

119
00:06:35.523 --> 00:06:38.424
"I won't," said Anne.

120
00:06:39.005 --> 00:06:41.446
Matthew left, surprised by his success.

121
00:06:42.206 --> 00:06:44.568
Then Anne leaned over the stair banisters.

122
00:06:46.028 --> 00:06:47.509
"Marilla, I'm ready to say sorry."

123
00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:49.651
Anne and Marilla went to Mrs.

124
00:06:49.711 --> 00:06:50.372
Lynde's house.

125
00:06:51.092 --> 00:06:53.875
As they walked, Anne did not look sorry.

126
00:06:54.475 --> 00:06:56.077
In fact, she looked very happy.

127
00:06:56.097 --> 00:06:58.118
"What are you thinking, Anne?"

128
00:06:58.659 --> 00:06:59.420
Marilla asked.

129
00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.082
"I'm thinking of what to say to Mrs.

130
00:07:02.162 --> 00:07:03.543
Lynde," Anne said.

131
00:07:04.184 --> 00:07:06.786
Marilla was suspicious but said nothing.

132
00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.048
As usual, Mrs.

133
00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:13.392
Lynde sat at the kitchen window, watching everything that went on outside the house.

134
00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.001
Anne suddenly kneeled in front of the surprised Mrs.

135
00:07:17.061 --> 00:07:18.241
Lynde and spoke.

136
00:07:18.261 --> 00:07:19.642
"Oh, Mrs.

137
00:07:19.762 --> 00:07:22.722
Lynde, I am so, so sorry.

138
00:07:23.303 --> 00:07:27.544
There are not enough words in the dictionary to say how sorry I am.

139
00:07:28.324 --> 00:07:33.825
What you said was true: my hair is red, and I'm freckled and skinny and ugly.

140
00:07:34.445 --> 00:07:37.566
What I said was true too, but I shouldn't have said it.

141
00:07:38.186 --> 00:07:40.827
Please, please, please forgive me."

142
00:07:41.567 --> 00:07:43.628
There was no doubt Anne was sincere.

143
00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.362
But unlike Marilla, Mrs.

144
00:07:46.442 --> 00:07:49.304
Lynde did not realize that Anne was also having fun.

145
00:07:50.024 --> 00:07:53.166
It was very dramatic, and Anne loved drama.

146
00:07:53.867 --> 00:07:56.769
Mrs. Lynde just said, "Get up, child.

147
00:07:57.549 --> 00:07:58.810
Of course I forgive you.

148
00:07:59.431 --> 00:08:04.094
Your hair is a terrible color, but maybe it will change when you grow up."

149
00:08:04.114 --> 00:08:06.295
"Oh, thank you, Mrs.

150
00:08:06.415 --> 00:08:07.736
Lynde," Anne said.

151
00:08:07.756 --> 00:08:09.477
"You give me hope!"

152
00:08:10.158 --> 00:08:11.459
With that, Mrs.

153
00:08:11.519 --> 00:08:12.800
Lynde was satisfied.
